{
 "daf": "31a",
 "kbVersion": "sha256-c91891f8b056f110",
 "sentences": {
  "0": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.1",
   "sugya": "berakhot_30b_vegilu_bireada",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_mar_tavar_kasa",
     "gloss_en": "Mar b. Ravina, at his son's wedding feast, seeing the Rabbanan very joyful, brought a precious cup worth four hundred zuz and broke it before them, and they became sad"
    }
   ]
  },
  "1": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.2",
   "sugya": "berakhot_30b_vegilu_bireada",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_rav_ashi_tavar_kasa",
     "gloss_en": "Rav Ashi, at his son's wedding feast, seeing the Rabbanan very joyful, brought a cup of white glass and broke it before them, and they became sad"
    }
   ]
  },
  "2": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.3",
   "sugya": "berakhot_30b_vegilu_bireada",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_vai_lan_dmitnan",
     "gloss_en": "woe to us, for we shall die; woe to us, for we shall die"
    }
   ]
  },
  "3": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.4",
   "sugya": "berakhot_30b_vegilu_bireada",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_assur_mele_schok",
     "gloss_en": "one is forbidden to fill his mouth with laughter in this world"
    }
   ]
  },
  "18": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.19",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_bayit_chalonot",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_shenemar_kavin",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "שנאמר וכוין פתיחן ליה -- Daniel prayed in an upper room with open windows",
     "supports": "p_bayit_chalonot",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_bayit_chalonot",
     "gloss_en": "one should always pray in a house that has windows"
    }
   ]
  },
  "19": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.20",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_bayit_chalonot",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mefurash_zimnin_tlata",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "כבר מפורש על ידי דניאל: וזמנין תלתא",
     "supports": "p_zimnin_tlata",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_zimnin_tlata",
     "gloss_en": "one might think a person may pray the whole day long; it is already explicit through Daniel [that it is three times]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "20": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.21",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_bayit_chalonot",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_neemar_kadmat_dna",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "כבר נאמר: די הוא עבד מן קדמת דנא",
     "supports": "p_min_kadmat_dna",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_min_kadmat_dna",
     "gloss_en": "one might think [Daniel's fixed prayer] began only when he came to the exile; [it is stated: he did so before]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "21": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.22",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_bayit_chalonot",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_talmud_lomar_neged",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "תלמוד לומר: נגד ירושלם",
     "supports": "p_neged_yerushalayim",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_neged_yerushalayim",
     "gloss_en": "one might think a person may pray toward any direction he wishes; [the verse says: toward Jerusalem]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "22": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.23",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_bayit_chalonot",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mefurash_david",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "כבר מפורש על ידי דוד, דכתיב: ערב ובקר וצהרים",
     "supports": "p_lo_kolelan",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_lo_kolelan",
     "gloss_en": "one might think he may include [the three prayers] all at once; it is already explicit through David [that they are evening, morning and noon]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "23": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.24",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_bayit_chalonot",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mefurash_chana",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "כבר מפורש על ידי חנה, שנאמר: וקולה לא ישמע",
     "supports": "p_lo_yashmia_kolo",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_lo_yashmia_kolo",
     "gloss_en": "one might think he may make his voice heard in his prayer; it is already explicit through Hannah [that he may not]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "24": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.25",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_bayit_chalonot",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mefurash_shlomo",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "כבר מפורש על ידי שלמה, שנאמר: לשמע אל הרנה ואל התפלה -- song before prayer",
     "supports": "p_tefilla_kodem_tzrachim",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_rina_zo_tefilla",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "רנה זו תפלה -- the first-named 'song' is prayer",
     "supports": "p_tefilla_kodem_tzrachim",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_tefilla_zo_bakasha",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "תפלה זו בקשה -- the second-named 'prayer' is request",
     "supports": "p_tefilla_kodem_tzrachim",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_tefilla_kodem_tzrachim",
     "gloss_en": "one might think a person asks for his needs and afterwards prays; it is already explicit through Solomon [that prayer comes first]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "25": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.26",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_bayit_chalonot",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_itmar_nami_rav",
     "kind": "mesaya",
     "gloss_en": "איתמר נמי: Rav too said that after his prayer one may say even the order of Yom Kippur",
     "supports": "p_achar_hatefilla_vidui",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_shoel_beshomea_tefilla",
     "gloss_en": "[the Sages] said: a person asks for his needs in 'who hears prayer'"
    }
   ]
  },
  "11": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.12",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_shekein_matzinu_neviim",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "שכן מצינו בנביאים הראשונים שסיימו דבריהם בדברי שבח ותנחומים (kind svara: no SupportKind names a שכן מצינו precedent)",
     "supports": "p_perida_mitoch_dvar_halacha",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_perida_lo_mitoch_sicha",
     "gloss_en": "likewise one should not take leave of his fellow from conversation"
    }
   ]
  },
  "13": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.14",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_ki_ha_derav_kahana",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "כי הא דרב כהנא אלוייה לרב שימי בר אשי -- at the end of the escort, Rav Shimi parted from him with R' Yosei b'R' Chanina's teaching (kind svara: the corpus's כי הא precedent shape)",
     "supports": "p_perida_mitoch_dvar_halacha",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_levayat_rav_kahana",
     "gloss_en": "Rav Kahana escorted Rav Shimi bar Ashi from Pum Nahara as far as the palm groves of Babylonia"
    }
   ]
  },
  "4": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.5",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_lo_mitoch_din",
     "gloss_en": "one may not stand to pray directly from [deciding] a judgment"
    }
   ]
  },
  "6": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.7",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_example_r_zeira",
     "gloss_en": "Abaye: a settled halakha is like R' Zeira's [on the daughters of Israel]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "7": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.8",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_example_rav_hoshaya",
     "gloss_en": "Rava: a settled halakha is like Rav Hoshaya's [on grain in its chaff]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "8": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.9",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_example_rav_huna",
     "gloss_en": "or say: a settled halakha is like Rav Huna's [in R' Ze'eira's name, on blood let from a consecrated animal]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "9": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.10",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_rabbanan_kematnitin",
     "gloss_en": "the Rabbanan acted like our mishnah [rising to pray from gravity]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "10": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.11",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_lo_mitoch_atzvut",
     "gloss_en": "one may not stand to pray from sadness"
    }
   ]
  },
  "12": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.13",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_mitoch_kach_zochrehu",
     "gloss_en": "for thereby he will remember him"
    }
   ]
  },
  "14": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.15",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_gazar_adam_harishon",
     "gloss_en": "'a land through which no man passed and where no man [adam] dwelt' (Jer 2:6) -- if none passed, how could any dwell? rather: every land Adam decreed for settlement was settled, and every land he did not was not"
    }
   ]
  },
  "15": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.16",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_halacha_pesuka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_levayat_rav_mordechai_bei_keifei",
     "gloss_en": "Rav Mordechai escorted Rav Shimi bar Ashi from Hagronya as far as Bei Keifei"
    }
   ]
  },
  "26": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.27",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_hilchot_chana",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mikan_al_liba",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "מכאן -- Hannah spoke in her heart",
     "supports": "p_mechaven_libo_chana",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mikan_sfateha",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "מכאן -- her lips moved",
     "supports": "p_chituch_sefatayim",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mikan_vekolah",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "מכאן -- her voice was not heard",
     "supports": "p_asur_lehagbia_kolo",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mikan_leshikora",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "מכאן -- Eli thought her drunk, i.e. had she been drunk her prayer would have been improper",
     "supports": "p_shikor_asur_lehitpallel",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_mechaven_libo_chana",
     "gloss_en": "'and Hannah spoke in her heart' -- from here, one who prays must direct his heart"
    }
   ]
  },
  "27": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.28",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_hilchot_chana",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mikan_ad_matai",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "מכאן -- Eli rebuked what he took for an unseemly thing",
     "supports": "p_tzarich_lehochicho",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_tzarich_lehochicho",
     "gloss_en": "from here, one who sees in his fellow an unseemly thing must rebuke him"
    }
   ]
  },
  "16": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.17",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_mechaven_libo",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_siman_tachin_libam",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "סימן לדבר: תכין לבם תקשיב אזנך -- a sign, not a proof: where the heart is directed, the ear listens",
     "supports": "p_mechaven_libo",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_mechaven_libo",
     "gloss_en": "one who prays must direct his heart toward Heaven"
    }
   ]
  },
  "17": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.31a.18",
   "sugya": "berakhot_31a_mechaven_libo",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mipnei_torach_tzibbur",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "מפני טורח ציבור -- he shortened so as not to burden the congregation",
     "supports": "p_r_akiva_mekatzer",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_mipnei_kriot",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "וכל כך למה? מפני כריעות והשתחוויות",
     "supports": "p_r_akiva_mezavit_lezavit",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_r_akiva_mekatzer",
     "gloss_en": "this was R' Akiva's custom: when he prayed with the congregation he would shorten and go up"
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}